  "summary_en": "This node marks the start of a Flow simulation block in Copernicus. Flow runs simple 2D simulations of incompressible flowing liquid.",
  "inputs": [
    "color: RGBA layer of initial fluid colors; read on the first frame only",
    "v: UV layer of initial flow directions; read on the first frame only",
    "temperature (optional): Mono layer of initial fluid temperatures; read on the first frame only",
    "feedback: cable fed back to the next iteration; its structure must exactly match the Flow Block End input; read on the first frame only",
    "passthrough (optional): cable of layers computed outside the simulation and read every frame, useful for animated sources"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Block Path: path to the matching Flow Block End node, which must be at the same network level",
    "Buoyancy: strength of the internal buoyancy force; the temperature field is scaled by this value and added to the velocity",
    "Buoyancy Direction: direction in which higher temperatures move",
    "Correct Initial Velocity: pressure-projects incoming velocities so they represent valid fluid motion",
    "Layers to Advect: wire names of the layers advected by the velocity layer; the v layer is always advected"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "Flow requires DOP-level permissions; it is not available in Houdini Core, only in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education",
    "Time Shift cannot be used inside Copernicus blocks when it needs block inputs at different times; the page suggests Time Pack before Block Begin, wired in as a cable",
    "Passthrough inputs cannot depend on the simulation results",
    "Operations that do not depend on previous frames should go before the block so they cook only once"
  ],
  "resume_fr": "Le nœud Flow Block Begin ouvre un bloc de simulation de fluide incompressible dans Copernicus, en fournissant les données initiales."
